
README
------

The VAMDC Species Database node,

Data ingestion cron job script:
update_content.sh, which runs node/cronjob.py (python 3, django environment)
then restarts the species service (server/server.py).



Data ingestion
--------------

node/cronjob.py runs the following steps:

1. update_nodes()             : read the VAMDC registry, add new nodes and update
                                the existing ones (vamdc_nodes)
2. query_active_nodes()       : for each node with update_status = active, send a
                                "SELECT Species" request and load the atoms and
                                molecules it returns
3. check_deprecated_species() : mark as deprecated the species not returned by a
                                node for more than 45 days
4. fill_search_table()        : empty and refill vamdc_merged_fields_vals, the table
                                used by the species service for searches

Each species returned by a node is loaded by load_atom() / load_molecule()
(node/import_functions.py) :

    verify  ->  vamdc_species  ->  vamdc_species_names  ->  vamdc_species_struct_formulae
            ->  vamdc_node_species

Rules applied during the import :

- Each species is loaded in a single transaction : if any step fails, nothing
  is written for this species, the error is printed and the import continues
  with the next one. This requires InnoDB tables (no transaction with MyISAM).

- InChI : get_clean_inchi() adds the "InChI=" prefix if missing and strips
  spaces. A species whose InChI does not start with "InChI=1" is rejected
  (ValueError) before anything is written.

- Missing structural formula (OrdinaryStructuralFormula, e.g. VALD molecules) :
  accepted, vamdc_node_species.database_species_formula is left NULL.

- Missing mass (MolecularWeight / MassNumber) : the mass computed from the InChI
  by OpenBabel is used, in vamdc_species.mass_number and in
  vamdc_node_species.member_database_mass_number (which can not be NULL).

- Deprecation : a vamdc_node_species row is deprecated when the species has not
  been seen for 45 days after the last node update. It is reactivated
  (deprecated = 0) as soon as the node returns the species again.

- Search table : only species having at least one vamdc_node_species row with
  deprecated = 0 are added to vamdc_merged_fields_vals. A species that is in
  vamdc_species but not in this table can not be found on the web site.



Debugging the import of a species
---------------------------------

node/debug_species.py replays the import of a single species from a node, using
the same functions as the cron job. It prints the data returned by the node,
the vamdc_node_species row that would be created, or the error that occurred.
All database changes are rolled back at the end (InnoDB only).

    cd /home/vamdc/NodeSoftware/nodes/VamdcSpeciesDB
    DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=settings \
        /home/vamdc/miniconda3/envs/django3.1/bin/python3 \
        node/debug_species.py <inchikey> [<node ivo identifier>]

    example :
        ... node/debug_species.py APKBIZXUJLWQRU-UHFFFAOYSA-N ivo://vamdc/vald/uu/all

The node identifier defaults to ivo://vamdc/vald/uu/all (VALD).

Useful queries :

    -- species without any link to a node (never visible on the web site)
    SELECT vs.id, vs.inchi, vs.stoichiometric_formula
    FROM vamdc_species vs
    LEFT JOIN vamdc_node_species vns ON vns.species_id = vs.id
    WHERE vns.id IS NULL;

    -- links between a species and the nodes
    SELECT vn.short_name, vn.status, vns.deprecated,
           vns.last_seen_dateTime, vn.last_update_date
    FROM vamdc_species vs
    JOIN vamdc_node_species vns ON vns.species_id = vs.id
    JOIN vamdc_nodes vn ON vn.id = vns.member_database_id
    WHERE vs.inchikey = '<inchikey>';



Exporting the data into sqlite database:
export_sqlite.sh in the VamdcSpeciesDB directory, using the helper scripts and export model in the export/ directory.

Once the export model is changed, please remove export/migrations contents and run
    ./manage.py makemigrations export to recreate the exported data model.

The data is exported into speciesdb.sqlite
